WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.069
Where I come from

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:06.970
we had to fight for a free press.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.130
I was born and raised in a military dictatorship

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.030
with just one TV channel

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.410
and a few newspapers with official information.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.560
But that dictator, Pinochet in Chile,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.119
couldn’t handle the critical work of brave
journalists

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:24.849
who dared to ask the right questions at the
right time.

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:28.329
As a journalist I have walked through the
streets of many countries

00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:31.089
and the problems are always the same:

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:33.560
poverty, social inequality,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.370
lack of freedom of the press

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.680
and corruption.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.239
One of our responsibilities as journalists
is

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:45.559
to face those in power,  those that make decisions for the
people.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.520
Asking, demanding the truth,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.040
for those who can’t or who are not allowed.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.019
We can’t afford to stay silent

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.289
when it comes to the defense of human and
civil rights

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.989
of those that have decided

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:00.560
to put their trust in us.

